Q1) 
i) Deadlock occurs when:
P1 locks R1
P2 locks R2
After 100 ms:
P1 requests R2, but R2 is already locked by P2
P2 requests R1, but R1 is already locked by P1
Both processes wait forever
This creates a Circular Wait condition
ii) OPTIMIZATION:
Use a Fixed Resource Ordering
Both processes should acquire resources in the same order
Use try-lock with timeout.
Use deadlock detection and recovery
Use single global lock if appropriate

